// UI strings for the 4 launch languages (backend V1_LANGUAGES = en/kn/te/hi).
// English is the source of truth: `Dict` is derived from it, so TypeScript
// refuses to compile if kn/te/hi miss a key. Strings that already existed in
// the previous app (urgency, scan source, disease actions, bug report, auth)
// reuse their previously-reviewed translations; the rest are new in Module 39
// and need a native-speaker read-through before a public release.
//
// What is NOT translated here, on purpose: advisory bodies and the
// "why this?" rationale text. Those are English sentences generated by the
// backend; only the audio route translates them (via the voice service).
// The UI says so where it matters (`englishOnly`).

